            <ArticleTitle>[Histiocytosis X with mandibular involvement. Apropos of a case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>31-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a case report of mandibular Histiocytosis X in its Eosinophilic Granuloma's form. A review of literature is realized in the two clinical forms of Histiocytosis X: localised forms, with insistance in the Eosinophilic Granuloma of jaws, and diffused forms represented by the Letterer-Siwe disease and the Hand-Schüller-Christian disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
